<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:40:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Brazil's tense presidential run-off campaign feels like a psychological thriller</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faa64628fc0054db6ee7d770346625b25a71fb2e6321a4ea6457b82d6eed0f1b</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:37:45Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T12:45:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller--934b659fa2c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-brazil-s-tense-presidential-run-off-campaign-feels-like-a-psychological-thriller" /><summary type="html">Insults traded on social media and a combative debate have intensified the pressure ahead of a fiercely contested presidential run-off on Sunday, with only a few points separating leftist pro-union President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and far-right challenger Flavio Bolsonaro, the son of former president and Trump ally Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>United-States : Backlash over controversial Ohio midterms campaign ad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b845922df0f5bd41d6c508c8bb370caaf188dd00cb54210c5cf516e141ba97b7</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:24Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T08:04:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/united-states-backlash-over-controversial-ohio-midterms-campaign-ad--5240dc639fc2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/united-states-backlash-over-controversial-ohio-midterms-campaign-ad" /><summary type="html">The backlash over an Ohio campaign advertisement attacking Amy Acton, the Democratic nominee for governor, spread beyond the state's borders Thursday, causing fresh headaches for Republicans with less than two weeks until the midterm elections.</summary></entry><entry><title>🇧🇷 Brazil: Why should you care about the country's elections?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2747237bb158a462c3f8eea7b0b12b4c9fa72197c7f554fafe9df70beb5895a3</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T06:48:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-brazil-why-should-you-care-about-the-country-s-elections--cb8adc17f6e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261023-brazil-why-should-you-care-about-the-country-s-elections" /><summary type="html">🗳️ On October 25, a runoff election in #Brazil could change the political landscape of #LatinAmerica. In the first round, #FlavioBolsonaro, son of ex-president Jair #Bolsonaro, beat incumbent President Luiz Inacio #Lula da Silva by a little over two million votes.
 
👉 But why should you care about who will win this second round? Our journalist Vitoria Barreto explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>New York City votes to ban Central Park horse-drawn carriages after decades of debate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf69494a46960a7cdf3b74e91495a2013c3ccaeaac96905288d83e607a30fd65</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:30Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T00:18:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-new-york-city-votes-to-ban-central-park-horse-drawn-carriages-after-decades-of-debate--1d892a705666.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261023-new-york-city-votes-to-ban-central-park-horse-drawn-carriages-after-decades-of-debate" /><summary type="html">New York's city council voted Thursday in favor of a measure to ban horse-drawn carriages in Central Park, a tourist attraction that has been controversial for years. Mayor Zohran Mamdani is expected to sign the ban into law which would go into effect starting in June 2028</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Emirati diplomat could become next UN chief despite human rights concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73e53d306da421f5cef3d86517cd5c9444f94549aab4cbdefa92a4fcc05ae636</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T21:18:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-emirati-diplomat-could-become-next-un-chief-despite-human-rights-concerns-uae-sudan-un-secr--36fc529e3344.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-emirati-diplomat-could-become-next-un-chief-despite-human-rights-concerns-uae-sudan-un-secretary-general-lana-nusseibeh" /><summary type="html">Human rights defenders are sounding the alarm over the United Arab Emirates’ nomination of its former envoy Lana Nusseibeh to be the next UN Secretary General. They say electing a diplomat from the UAE, a country with a questionable human rights record that is accused of backing forces behind a massacre in Sudan, could spell “catastrophe” for the UN.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Vance tells Republicans to 'stop whining' after Ramaswamy attack ad in Ohio governor's race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8531a460090e1992bfb353aeeeffdbadc1129e29026f217a81208cdf467b60cf</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T19:05:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/vance-tells-republicans-to-stop-whining-after-ramaswamy-attack-ad-in-ohio-governor-s-race--58bc4a1ae869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/vance-tells-republicans-to-stop-whining-after-ramaswamy-attack-ad-in-ohio-governor-s-race" /><summary type="html">US Vice President JD Vance on Wednesday defended an explosive attack ad by Republican Vivek Ramaswamy’s campaign against his Democratic rival in the Ohio governor’s race, telling fellow Republicans to "stop whining" about it and go win the race. The ad features ​Democrat Amy Acton’s ‌estranged mother, Donna Arthur, disputing Acton’s account of a childhood she says involved a period of homelessness and sexual abuse. ⁠Arthur, whom Acton says she has not seen since 1978, urges Ohioans not to vote for her daughter. Acton has said she was sexually abused by her stepfather when she was 12. Her mother stayed with the ‌stepfather, who was charged with rape but fled the state and was never tried. He died in 2004. Acton said she ⁠and her brother were removed from her mother's custody for severe abuse, neglect and sexual abuse. Acton's brother has supported her account. FRANCE 24's Catherine Viette reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Back to the Bolsonaros? Brazil's presidential run-off goes down to the wire</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:683289d116f5f48e06e7ec198d35273a4d005cf50ba10c44f336edf12744dc8e</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T18:18:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-back-to-the-bolsonaros-brazil-presidential-run-off-goes-down-to-the-wire--976659f1cff7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261022-back-to-the-bolsonaros-brazil-presidential-run-off-goes-down-to-the-wire" /><summary type="html">Brazil's future is within the margin of error ahead of Sunday's presidential runoff: most of the latest polls put the far-right's Flavio Bolsonaro ahead of left-wing incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva – a lead that's narrowed after last weekend's acrimonious debate.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Ahead of US and Israeli elections, 3-day joint attack on Iran 'would not radically change conflict'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:70bcf6dec287c1bb7201f3c1610c3609474fbc9d3c6d85bb4f241965f7b0d195</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:12Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T16:36:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict--cb0fe2d52092.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ahead-of-us-and-israeli-elections-3-day-joint-attack-on-iran-would-not-radically-change-conflict" /><summary type="html">Jean-Emile Jammine is pleased to welcome Federico Donelli, Associate Professor of International Relations in the Department of Political and Social Sciences at the University of Trieste in Italy. Can another three days of military strikes achieve what eight months of confrontation have failed to deliver? Donelli challenges the assumption that a short, intensive offensive would necessarily produce a decisive political outcome. He argues, "the real question is whether military pressure is intended to constrain Iran's capacity, or to pressure Iran to sit on the table." And whether they can translate that capacity into a sustainable political outcome without provoking a wider regional crisis. Regardless, Donelli reminds us that "Iran still has leverage over the US."</summary></entry><entry><title>Georgia on Democrats’ minds: Powering up the Black vote to counter Trump's meddling</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f6a5551fb2f421b1e00f6821f8ca448099f3987c134893d1bdf6b11b92f12e7</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T15:43:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-georgia-on-democrats-minds-powering-up-black-vote-counter-trump-meddling--7648a88f5f00.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261022-georgia-on-democrats-minds-powering-up-black-vote-counter-trump-meddling" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump's push to redistrict congressional maps and a Georgia state election law disproportionately affecting African Americans are aimed at diluting the power of the Black vote. Six decades after Atlanta was at the heart of the civil rights movement that granted Blacks in the southern states the right to vote, the community is fighting back.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's sprawling favelas require long-term urban planning solutions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:085b8d5d9d75128d9b0af68726a44f772f7f058f05e1b4688ce65a0bc597e3f3</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:46Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T12:31:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261022-brazil-s-sprawling-favelas-require-long-term-urban-planning-solutions--4857e607d4ea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261022-brazil-s-sprawling-favelas-require-long-term-urban-planning-solutions" /><summary type="html">As Brazilians head to the polls on Sunday for the second round of presidential elections, our correspondents take us to the heart of the country's favelas, where residents live in unsanitary conditions. Over the past 40 years, the area occupied by Brazilian favelas has almost tripled in size. They now cover around 460,000 hectares, compared with 53,700 in 1985.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump admin 'destroying' US democracy with 'autocratic, terrorist version of Christian nationalism'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61228d6eb49f39adbcb6c88cbf439ca98c65e0b269b574d5d7dd2fed399068a6</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T22:11:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-national--f98b028aa6cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261021-trump-admin-destroying-us-democracy-with-autocratic-terrorist-version-of-christian-nationalism" /><summary type="html">François Picard welcomes former US Assistant Secretary of Defense Jim Townsend and former US Air Force officer Michael (Mikey) Weinstein, founder and president of the Military Religious Freedom Foundation. Is American military power becoming an instrument of political and religious coercion, both at home and abroad? From the reported restrictions on Ukraine's access to Starlink satellite communications to the Trump administration's overtures towards Russian President Vladimir Putin and the growing controversy over religious ideology within the Pentagon, the two guests offer a stark assessment of the direction of American foreign and defence policy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Trump exploits France riots to push false immigration claims ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3487def1fa0a4d2f2fe14b10e1da6090e7c07ef4fea96c0e0c04aaa6e1c1349b</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:28:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms--d75f9c282915.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261021-trump-uses-france-riots-to-push-false-immigration-claims-ahead-of-midterms" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump and his inner circle are using unrest in France to push unsubstantiated claims blaming the riots on immigration, even showing French protest footage at midterm rallies. But there is no evidence linking immigration to the unrest, and it's prompted French President Emmanuel Macron to accuse world leaders of making "stupid comments" at France's expense. Trump's focus comes as Republicans face mounting pressure ahead of the midterms and his approval rating hits a reported record low.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Some Brazilians long associated with the left now shift towards Flavio Bolsonaro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:780c02777b1dfb80af79772c64cf5b20a4e8af14a868f1ee1776aeafff5fe72c</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T15:28:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro--276f6e2ecc23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-some-brazilians-long-associated-with-the-left-now-shift-towards-flavio-bolsonaro" /><summary type="html">In the first round of Brazil’s presidential elections, Flavio Bolsonaro got the most votes in 15 electoral districts in the North Zone of Rio de Janeiro, compared with 9 for Lula. This part of the city, long associated with the left and the social policies of Lula’s Workers’ Party, is now shifting towards former president Jair Bolsonaro’s son.</summary></entry><entry><title>Peter Zalmayev: 'Ukraine was showing all sorts of cards that Trump took away and gave to Putin'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:84fb116eb352c83f61e06317b6c28cb55e5c7968cb16db76daf952a89d87e368</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:39:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin---0e5c90a4d0ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261021-ukraine-was-showing-all-sorts-of-cards-that-trump-took-away-from-ukraine-and-gave-to-putin-1" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Peter Zalmayev, Founder and Director of the Eurasia Democracy Initiative, LIVE from Kyiv. And he warns, "I'm seeing, I'm smelling a Yalta II. I'm smelling another Munich (1938), where we're seeing appeasement of the aggressor." Ukraine faces the possibility that its sovereignty and security could become mere bargaining chips in an era Zalmayev describes as great-power "collusion". He delivers a forceful critique of the Trump administration's approach to Russia, arguing that Washington is weakening Ukraine's negotiating position while offering Vladimir Putin little incentive to abandon his maximalist demands. At stake, he suggests, are the cohesion of the transatlantic alliance, and the credibility of Western security commitments.</summary></entry><entry><title>Concerns mount over artificial intelligence as Silicon Valley sees AI boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e750603ff62a687d16e073b2c75b8d3a16925c727c1c74d709141c69d6204b18</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:40:01Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:15:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261021-concerns-mount-over-artificial-intelligence-as-silicon-valley-sees-ai-boom--fb07f401c7af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261021-concerns-mount-over-artificial-intelligence-as-silicon-valley-sees-ai-boom" /><summary type="html">Tuesday, October 20 saw protests in more than 50 US cities against the rise of artificial intelligence. Demonstrators are calling for a moratorium on AI development, and the sentiment is shared by many: according to a recent study, 71 percent of Americans believe AI will lead to job losses. In the heart of Silicon Valley, record investment is now on a collision course with public fear and uncertainty. FRANCE 24's Pierrick Leurent and Valérie Defert report, with Wassim Cornet.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Trump campaigns in deep-red states, fearing Democratic wave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:840d8c538fe97ec0ef7d99bc3df60b44b0c18fa8ffae585c29901dfebd6f3651</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:51:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigns-in-deep-red-states-fearing-democratic-wave--f35171296156.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigns-in-deep-red-states-fearing-democratic-wave" /><summary type="html">The midterm elections are just two weeks away in the United States and Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Polls showing support for the Republican Party is slipping drastically, even in some deep red states. Story by Monte Francis.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI on the ballot? Voters in US midterms revolt against data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6c7dbca9de2b903426a839b31226f4e65605c7bccdc2a36a8054a7290c8c884</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T22:45:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-ai-on-the-ballot-voters-in-us-midterms-revolt-against-data-centres--00ec068c2493.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261020-ai-on-the-ballot-voters-in-us-midterms-revolt-against-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Two weeks out from the US midterm elections, there's bipartisan pushback against data centres that suck the water and power out of communities. Just two years ago, ChatGPT was still a brand-new thing, and AI was admired with awe by most voters. Like in 2024, the hot-button issue in swing constituencies remains inflation, or "the price of eggs". But anxiety over the end of the month is now coupled with anxiety over the end of the world.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil’s presidential candidates push to have one another disqualified ahead of run-off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e033b594643cb9629e15aa9f54a97d81069a4dd77dd4fb7b8fbeaa8c5a25f4</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T20:59:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261020-lula-campaign-seeks-disqualify-bolsonoro-from-brazil-presidential-vote-over-meta-interferen--28674a91421b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261020-lula-campaign-seeks-disqualify-bolsonoro-from-brazil-presidential-vote-over-meta-interference" /><summary type="html">Both candidates in Brazil's presidential election called for their rival's disqualification Tuesday over allegations of social media malfeasance, according to court filings. Left-wing President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s campaign said they will request the annulment of right-wing rival Flavio Bolsonaro's candidacy over alleged election interference by tech giant Meta, while Bolsonaro's team is accusing Lula of "abuse of power" in the mass sharing of government postings on WhatsApp.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump campaigning in Republican strongholds amid slide in polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:639dc70bd3bb36f3239a12182e0d47619f9fd28b8d8b9f5d98a6943bc12f3b0f</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T20:13:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigning-in-republican-strongholds-amid-slide-in-polls--38598da6800a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-campaigning-in-republican-strongholds-amid-slide-in-polls" /><summary type="html">With the midterm elections fast approaching, US President Donald Trump is stumping for candidates in states that he won by double digits in 2024. Despite what he says, it’s a sign of what Trump and the Republican party are fearing: with polls showing GOP support slip drastically even in some deep red states. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US midterm elections: Trump approval rating falls to new low</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:808264121104f1322c8856c599a6e155a1dd2690c7f57513e0e3200632c948e1</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T15:22:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-us-midterm-elections-trump-approval-rating-falls-to-new-low--bc210483afa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261020-us-midterm-elections-trump-approval-rating-falls-to-new-low" /><summary type="html">With US President Donald Trump’s approval rating falling to a record low of 31%, Republicans are facing mounting concerns ahead of November’s midterm elections. Republicans are at risk of losing control of the House of Representatives, but how big could the Democrats’ gains be? FRANCE 24’s International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Alberta votes to remain part of Canada in victory for PM Carney</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8c24bed2784b83638e045194cca86113123c78dbed98c09533bb92d1aaff988</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:45:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-alberta-votes-to-remain-part-of-canada-in-victory-for-pm-carney--80a5f9f09a54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-alberta-votes-to-remain-part-of-canada-in-victory-for-pm-carney" /><summary type="html">Voters in oil-rich Alberta overwhelmingly backed remaining in Canada in the province's first-ever referendum on separation, with early results on Tuesday delivering a boost to Prime Minister Mark Carney’s push for national unity amid US President Donald Trump’s trade war and annexation threats.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Four soldiers dead, dozens injured in fire at Canada military base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f7f01d9e85f0cba8c17958ef246534fe30fa8cffad3080f04acc81c1f301c79</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:25:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-four-soldiers-dead-dozens-injured-in-fire-at-canada-military-base--5b7bd85ac81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-four-soldiers-dead-dozens-injured-in-fire-at-canada-military-base" /><summary type="html">Four soldiers were killed and dozens injured in a fire at a military base in Alberta province, one of the worst peacetime tragedies to hit Canada's armed forces on home soil, Prime Minister Mark Carney said Sunday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Brazil court orders Meta to prove it gives Lula, Bolsonaro campaign content equal treatment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:41392ba3c3e49eddb23cb56c31a125345b3192b29e59ecb5eb4fc93139c29ae1</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T14:16:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-court-orders-meta-prove-gives-lula-bolsonaro-campaign-content-equal-treatment--983975c9bef7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-court-orders-meta-prove-gives-lula-bolsonaro-campaign-content-equal-treatment" /><summary type="html">Brazil’s top electoral court has given Meta 24 hours to prove it is treating campaign content from incumbent President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Senator Flavio Bolsonaro equally on its online platforms, threatening a daily fine for noncompliance. The ruling follows allegations from Lula's campaign that the social media giant is suppressing Lula’s campaign content ahead of Sunday’s closely contested presidential runoff.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil's Lula, Bolsonaro clash in bitter debate ahead of election run-off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dca9171087e715a46b72b3e7ad4068ea1cfdf84474b0013b7b68e8682f9ea5a6</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-19T03:42:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-lula-bolsonaro-debate-election-runoff--dc34142a5ff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261019-brazil-lula-bolsonaro-debate-election-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and right-wing senator Flavio Bolsonaro traded personal attacks in a heated presidential debate on Sunday, a week before a closely contested run-off. The rivals accused each other of lying and corruption while clashing over the economy, security and healthcare ahead of the October 25 vote.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian military base fire kills at least four, injures dozens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e41c474c4db807c3dcd73b4780915de0c75b9d9c0f472d1dd3d14656d6265128</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T22:16:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised--e89b96884cf2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-canada-military-base-fire-four-dead-39-hospitalised" /><summary type="html">Four Canadian service members were killed and 39 people hospitalised after a fire broke out during military training at a base in Alberta on Saturday, officials said. Premier Danielle Smith said Sunday that at least 19 patients were in critical condition, with some suffering severe burns requiring prolonged intensive treatment.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Atlanta’s iconic tavern marks Georgia’s past with an eye on future as midterms approach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:904c51ae3c99538b6e05b9460f3063c7aed8d54bb79401a6b9b16181e4c6f1dc</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T11:15:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-atlanta-iconic-tavern-marks-georgia-past-eye-future-midterms-approach-ossoff-collins--07358f3ce484.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-atlanta-iconic-tavern-marks-georgia-past-eye-future-midterms-approach-ossoff-collins" /><summary type="html">Since it was established in 1956, Manuel’s Tavern in Atlanta has hosted legendary Democratic leaders while its founder played a key role in the city’s move from a Republican to Democratic stronghold. With the state’s Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff leading the polls in the midterms amid rumours of a future presidential run, the tavern is once more at the heart of the political action.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Rubio says Trump to 'analyze' global impact of Russia sanctions during pause</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b93c8f4f38f154aa7e966799c5a946d8a1825d10c6f0086e86098800d13161a9</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T02:39:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact--05ec5cb4d55f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact" /><summary type="html">US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that US President Donald Trump’s decision to waive sanctions and tariffs on Russia would last 60 days, as the move drew bipartisan criticism and raised fears in Ukraine that Washington could ease further restrictions on Moscow.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘Standing up for democracy’: Atlanta ‘No Kings’ rally draws Trump critics ahead of midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e95b570ed2116a1cb5608edc0973578b76eb0b60518ab902fc86d324f815bb12</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-18T01:50:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms--d077ded60ac1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">“No Kings, Vote Now” was the theme of a rally in Atlanta, one of many organised across the US on Saturday. While many demonstrators denounced US President Donald Trump’s policies, organisers said the rally was aimed at getting out the vote in the November 3 midterm elections and protecting democracy in America.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Embattled new White House Press Secretary Zacharia 'let go' from her role</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:338f22e50acf194d18b98621691c3d8c9d48bf2c2d5deb06ec8b639572856a73</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T15:57:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role--b8377cd6b5ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261016-embattled-new-white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-let-go-from-her-role" /><summary type="html">A White House Press official said Friday that Secretary ​Katie Zacharia was "let go" from her role after US President Donald Trump signaled she was on her way out, a week after he picked her for the post. Zacharia's credentials as an attorney had come under scrutiny and she admitted to not having passed the bar in an interview with Fox News on Thursday.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Thanks a lot, Trump': Wyoming conservatives divided ahead of US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9dacb166367f6ef2e8f1249ccde83861a76f64c8460b8e9cb37cb233c413272b</id><updated>2026-10-23T13:36:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T12:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms--9dc82ebe6bd5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261016-thanks-a-lot-trump-wyoming-conservatives-divided-ahead-us-midterms" /><summary type="html">Famous for its cowboy culture, Wyoming is the least populated, the most rural and the most conservative of all the US states. With two weeks to go until the midterm elections, our reporters James André and Sylvain Rousseau travelled across this Republican stronghold and found that the party of US President Donald Trump is deeply divided in the Cowboy State.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry></feed>
